          wrongTurn: 'The wrong turn is searching for colour instead of searching for meaning. Bright things get found, quiet distinctions survive the audit, and the list looks complete.',
          tradeoff: 'The meaning question is slower and produces items you will argue with yourself about, such as whether a slightly warmer row background is really carrying anything. Arguing about it is better than never listing it.',
